@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# GitHub readiness
+
+Use the extracted `gridsense/` directory as the repository root. It contains
+the workflow, lockfiles, tests, model provenance, third-party notices and
+documentation. See the [dated review](REVIEW_2026-10-14.md) for executed local
+checks and outstanding validation.
+
+## Included repository files
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.github/workflows/checks.yml` | Linux and Windows integration jobs with locked installation, dependency audit, lint, native tests, browser tests and runtime checks |
+| `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml` | Environment and reproducible steps for ordinary defects |
+| `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` | Change, validation and experiment-evidence record |
+| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Contributor setup, regression checks and replay identity |
+| `SECURITY.md` | Local-use scope and private vulnerability-reporting guidance |
+| `.gitignore` | Excludes environments, caches, built frontend and runtime data from the source repository |
+| `.gitattributes` | LF source identity and byte-exact bundled reference files |
+
+The source repository excludes `frontend/dist/`; `npm ci` and `npm run build`
+recreate it. The standalone release ZIP includes the verified build. The
+release packager also excludes SQLite databases and their journal files in
+custom data directories, and retains contribution, security and license files
+when present.
+
+## Owner decisions and hosted checks
+
+The original GridSense source has no project-wide license. The owner must
+select the intended terms before an open-source release; the third-party
+licenses already included remain specific to their components.
+[GitHub's licensing guide](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/licensing-a-repository)
+explains adding a repository license.
+
+Windows execution and GitHub-hosted CI remain unverified. The workflow is
+configured and its commands were exercised locally on Linux. After pushing,
+inspect both matrix jobs and their uploaded verification reports before
+marking those platforms verified. Private vulnerability reporting and branch
+protection are repository settings to configure after creation.
+
+## Push the prepared source
+
+Create an empty GitHub repository, then run these commands from `gridsense/`,
+after reviewing the intended license and files to commit. Replace the remote
+placeholder with your repository URL:
+
+```bash
+git init -b main
+git add .
+git status --short
+git commit -m "Add GridSense restoration simulator"
+git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_ACCOUNT/YOUR_REPOSITORY.git
+git push -u origin main
+```
+
+These commands are instructions for the owner. This review did not create,
+push or publish a remote repository.
